What is an Azure Virtual Network (VNet)?

A Virtual Network (VNet) is a logically isolated private network in Azure that enables Azure resources to communicate securely.

Think of it as your private data center network in the cloud.

Resources inside a VNet can communicate with each other using private IP addresses.

Examples:

Virtual Machines
AKS
Azure Bastion
Private Endpoints
Load Balancers
