Web    App          Database
Subnet Subnet       Subnet
Why Do We Need a VNet?

Without a VNet:

Resources communicate over public internet.
Less secure.

With a VNet:

Private communication.
Network isolation.
Better security.
Easier access control.
What is an Address Space?

An Address Space defines the range of private IP addresses available inside a VNet.

Example:

10.0.0.0/16

This means the VNet can allocate IPs from:

10.0.0.1
...
10.0.255.254
CIDR Notation

Azure uses CIDR (Classless Inter-Domain Routing).

Examples:

CIDR	Approx. Number of IPs
/24	256
/23	512
/22	1024
/21	2048
/20	4096
/16	65,536

Interview Tip: You don't need to memorize every value. Understand that a smaller prefix (e.g., /16) provides more IP addresses than a larger prefix (e.g., /24).

What is a Subnet?

A Subnet divides a VNet into smaller logical networks.

Example:

VNet
10.0.0.0/16

Split into:

Web Subnet
10.0.1.0/24

App Subnet
10.0.2.0/24

DB Subnet
10.0.3.0/24

Each subnet has its own IP range.

Why Use Subnets?

Benefits:

Security isolation
Better traffic management
Easier NSG application
Supports different application tiers
Reduces broadcast domains
