Azure Reserved IP Addresses

Azure reserves the first four IP addresses and the last IP address in every subnet.

Example:

Subnet
10.0.1.0/24

Reserved:

10.0.1.0
10.0.1.1
10.0.1.2
10.0.1.3
10.0.1.255

Usable IPs:

10.0.1.4
...
10.0.1.254

This is a common interview question.

Public vs Private IP
Public IP	Private IP
Internet accessible	Internal only
Assigned to gateways, load balancers, public VMs	Assigned inside a VNet
Globally routable	Not routable over the public internet
Hands-on Lab 1: Create a VNet
Azure Portal

Create:

Setting	Value
Resource Group	rg-az400-dev
Name	vnet-az400-dev
Address Space	10.0.0.0/16
Azure CLI
az network vnet create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --name vnet-az400-dev \
  --address-prefix 10.0.0.0/16

Verify:

az network vnet list --output table
Hands-on Lab 2: Create Subnets

Create:

Subnet	CIDR
Web	10.0.1.0/24
App	10.0.2.0/24
DB	10.0.3.0/24

CLI:

az network vnet subnet create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --vnet-name vnet-az400-dev \
  --name web-subnet \
  --address-prefixes 10.0.1.0/24

Repeat for:

app-subnet
10.0.2.0/24
db-subnet
10.0.3.0/24

Verify:

az network vnet subnet list \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --vnet-name vnet-az400-dev \
  --output table
